@startuml opcua_server_request_flow
!include _style.puml

title OPC UA server — request flow

participant "OPC UA client" as Client $external
participant "opcuapp Endpoint" as Endpoint $tier
participant "binary::ServiceDispatcher" as Dispatcher $tier
participant "binary::Runtime" as BinRt $tier
participant "opcua::ServerRuntime" as Runtime $neutral
participant "opcua_conversion" as Conv $neutral
participant "SCADA service" as Svc $tier

Client -> Endpoint : UA Binary request
Endpoint -> Dispatcher : decoded service payload
note right of Dispatcher
  Transport decode / adapter normalization
  happens at the Binary edge.
end note
Dispatcher -> BinRt : invoke decoded request
note right of BinRt
  Binary-only runtime work is limited to token lookup
  and authenticated dispatch over canonical opcua::
  request/response types.
end note
BinRt -> Runtime : canonical request dispatch
Runtime -> Conv : convert request payload
Conv --> Runtime : SCADA-native inputs
note right of Runtime
  Shared service dispatch lives in opcua::ServerRuntime
  and routes canonical requests into shared SCADA services.
end note
Runtime -> Svc : Read / Write / Browse / Call / AddNodes / DeleteNodes
Svc --> Runtime : status + results
Runtime -> Conv : convert results
Conv --> Runtime : OPC UA response payload
Runtime --> BinRt : canonical response
BinRt --> Dispatcher : Binary response body
note right of Dispatcher
  Response encoding / transport-specific exceptions
  stay wire-only, including HistoryReadEvents encoding.
end note
Dispatcher --> Endpoint : encoded Binary response
Endpoint --> Client : UA Binary response

@enduml
